From: =?UTF-8?q?Berkay=20K=C3=B6sebay?= <brkosebay@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 15:26:19 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] soc: apple: aop: name the sleep precheck refusal

Log that the AOP firmware has not started when the precheck refuses,
only during a suspend attempt. The decision is unchanged.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 drivers/soc/apple/aop.c | 7 ++++++-
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/soc/apple/aop.c b/drivers/soc/apple/aop.c
index f0ad4c87f..84ba67c59 100644
--- a/drivers/soc/apple/aop.c
+++ b/drivers/soc/apple/aop.c
@@ -1394,7 +1394,12 @@ static int apple_aop_sleep_precheck(struct notifier_block *nb, unsigned long act
 
 	if (action == PM_SUSPEND_PRECHECK_COMPLETE)
 		return NOTIFY_DONE;
-	return READ_ONCE(aop->sleep_ready) ? NOTIFY_OK : notifier_from_errno(-EBUSY);
+	if (READ_ONCE(aop->sleep_ready))
+		return NOTIFY_OK;
+	/* Only for an attempt: the readiness query polls this. */
+	if (data == PM_SUSPEND_PRECHECK_ATTEMPT)
+		dev_info(aop->dev, "system sleep refused: AOP firmware not started\n");
+	return notifier_from_errno(-EBUSY);
 }
 
 static void apple_aop_sleep_unregister(void *data)
